# perfcached.sysusers — systemd-sysusers(8) declaration (task S46).
#
# perfcached.service runs as User=perfcached, and a unit that names a
# user nothing creates fails to start with a message that points at
# systemd rather than at the missing account.  Install this as
# /usr/lib/sysusers.d/perfcached.conf and run:
#
#     systemd-sysusers
#
# A system account with no login shell and no home: the daemon needs
# neither, and its state directory is created by the unit's
# StateDirectory= (which also chowns it), not by a home directory.
#
# No tmpfiles.d file accompanies this on purpose - StateDirectory=
# already creates /var/lib/perfcached 0700 and owns it to this user,
# so a tmpfiles rule would be a second source of truth for the same
# path and they would drift.
u perfcached - "perfcached cache daemon" - -
